# Development only. No secrets are required for fixture runs.
# ML_ENVIRONMENT: development or test; production is rejected until pilot gates pass.
# ML_AUTH_MODE: demo by default; local_token enables the gated development control API.
# ML_CONTROL_API_ENABLED: false by default; true requires local_token and a public key path.
# ML_IDENTITY_PUBLIC_KEY_PATH: .local/identity/public.pem after `make identity-init`.
# ML_IDENTITY_ISSUER / ML_IDENTITY_AUDIENCE: pinned trusted local token values.
# ML_RUNNER_MODE: fixture for the retained Python reference only; customer execution is disabled.
# ML_DATABASE_URL: PostgreSQL connection, supplied outside source control.
# ML_MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL: separate migration role; never a runtime fallback.
# ML_ARTIFACT_ROOT: local immutable fictional evidence directory (default artifacts).
# ML_EMERGENCY_STOP: true disables new execution and publication.
